# Go invariants

- Mutable session config has one pointer owner: `MapExporter` stores the caller's `*MapExportConfig`; do not manually sync struct copies. Pass immutable one-shot snapshots by value.
- Factories whose results callers mutate return pointers (`AddDoodadType`). MDL graph nodes use shared pointers, wired at creation; merge remapping in `mergeItemObjects` remains necessary.
- Stable selection/export order uses ordered slices, with maps only for lookup. CASC `selectRootContentKey` prefers `ContentHighResTexture`; never select the first match from map iteration.
- Direct conversion stays typed and in memory; `File.LoadFromData` owns an isolated snapshot, including nested slices and nullable timestamps. See `docs/architecture.md` under "Trace a change before editing" for the metadata boundary.
- Propagate `job.Context()`; retain job capacity until handlers and started workers return, and discard late success after cancellation. Never reset shared CASC to cancel a job. Lifecycle details: `docs/architecture.md`, `server/util/jobqueue.go`, and `converter/common/worker_pool.go` (Go paths under `golang/internal/`).
